Job Code: JPC - 5983
Job Title: Manager, Web Platforms
Job Location: Abu Dhabi, UAE

Job Purpose:
Own the end-to-end development, performance, and continuous evolution of web platforms. The role combines full-stack engineering, UX/UI design, SEO, analytics, and platform security to deliver a secure, high-performing, and user-friendly digital experience while maintaining proper documentation and development best practices.

Job Description:
- Manage the full lifecycle of web platforms, including frontend and backend development, UX/UI optimization, SEO, analytics, integrations, deployment, and platform security.
- Work closely with stakeholders to enhance digital journeys, improve website performance, support CRM and admissions workflows, and ensure smooth deployment, scalability, and system stability.

Key Responsibilities:
- Develop and maintain end-to-end web applications using modern frameworks such as Next.js, React, Angular, or equivalent.
- Manage backend development, API integrations, and database connectivity.
- Lead UX/UI design enhancements including wireframing, prototyping, and user journey mapping.
- Own SEO strategy, discoverability, and web indexing best practices.
- Manage analytics, tracking tags, and advertising integrations.
- Monitor website performance, troubleshoot issues, and improve scalability and security.
- Collaborate with stakeholders on feature enhancements and platform updates.
- Manage workflows and funnels across web platforms.
- Support CRM setup and integrations including Zoho and HubSpot.
- Manage hosting, deployment systems, version control, and release workflows.
- Design and integrate APIs and third-party services.
- Implement web security best practices and compliance standards.
- Maintain technical documentation and development standards.
- Integrate AI solutions to enhance workflow productivity.
- Support team collaboration and web team culture initiatives.

Requirements:
- Strong experience in full-stack web development.
- Advanced JavaScript skills with modern frameworks.
- Experience in Node.js, Python, or similar backend technologies.
- Strong experience in API development.
- Hands-on knowledge of Git, deployment pipelines, and hosting environments.
- Experience with SQL or NoSQL databases.
- Solid understanding of web security and authentication.
- Experience with SEO tools, Google Analytics, and Tag Manager.
- Strong UX/UI design exposure.

